{
  "dom_id": "step-e4060",
  "name": "Example: Evaluating Common Logarithms of Fractions and Roots",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\log\\left( 0.1 \\right).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $0.1$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n0.1 = 10^{-1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 0.1 \\right) = \\log\\left(10^{-1}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm of a power of $10$ is the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log\\left(10^x\\right) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x = -1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 10^{-1} \\right)= -1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
